(4139543, 594595, 63503, '<td valign="top">Good idea, lighting is a bit puzzling as it a ppears to be harsh in both directions; if you used fill flash (it looks like you did) soft  boxes would have helped. Also, a from below or straight camera angle (instead of from above)would have been more flattering to the models that are kneeling down. Seeing that empty street and the cross walk lines I can''t help but wish you would have taken a Beatles like shot of the 5 girls walking accross the street in perfect coordination and looking straight ahead rather than at the camera, I would have given you a 10 for that one.</td>', 'Good idea, lighting is a bit puzzling as it a ppears to be harsh in both directions; if you used fill flash (it looks like you did) soft  boxes would have helped. Also, a from below or straight camera angle (instead of from above)would have been more flattering to the models that are kneeling down. Seeing that empty street and the cross walk lines I can''t help but wish you would have taken a Beatles like shot of the 5 girls walking accross the street in perfect coordination and looking straight ahead rather than at the camera, I would have given you a 10 for that one.', '2007-10-03 23:32:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(4139575, 594202, 63503, '<td valign="top">Funny !! I am sure you''ll p.o. a few. Photographicaly speaking, the light you placed to the right of or directly above the camera could have been less harsh; as it is, the blown out JC body is less than visually appealing. Also, the hair light is a bit too strong, in my opinion. A better image than most in this challenge though.</td>', 'Funny !! I am sure you''ll p.o. a few. Photographicaly speaking, the light you placed to the right of or directly above the camera could have been less harsh; as it is, the blown out JC body is less than visually appealing. Also, the hair light is a bit too strong, in my opinion. A better image than most in this challenge though.', '2007-10-03 23:40:31.000000', NULL, 1),
