(4156798, 594187, 40372, '<td valign="top">Thanks for your feedback, folks.<br/>The story in the photo is this: a group of guys (Norwegian, I think) were walking down the street, apparently after a few happy drinks. At one place they stopped and asked one of them to take a group picture. The guy dug out a compact and slowly and carefully lied down on the street to get a better angle. I happened to pass by and had a one second window to take the shot. So, the group was not posing for me, which may qualify the photo as a candid. On the other hand, they were laughing and looking straight into my lens, so there was nothing candid about the scene and the guys were quite easy about someone photographing them.<br/>I agree about tilt and all, but personally I like the spontaneity of the moment.<br/>Regards to all,<br/>Tarmo aka Didymus</td>', 'Thanks for your feedback, folks.The story in the photo is this: a group of guys (Norwegian, I think) were walking down the street, apparently after a few happy drinks. At one place they stopped and asked one of them to take a group picture. The guy dug out a compact and slowly and carefully lied down on the street to get a better angle. I happened to pass by and had a one second window to take the shot. So, the group was not posing for me, which may qualify the photo as a candid. On the other hand, they were laughing and looking straight into my lens, so there was nothing candid about the scene and the guys were quite easy about someone photographing them.I agree about tilt and all, but personally I like the spontaneity of the moment.Regards to all,Tarmo aka Didymus', '2007-10-10 08:23:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(4156803, 594451, 67152, '<td valign="top">Judi- I think there is a medicine to clear those spots up...<br/> <br/>Great photo!  Love the expressions, the lighting and the processing.</td>', 'Judi- I think there is a medicine to clear those spots up... Great photo!  Love the expressions, the lighting and the processing.', '2007-10-10 08:26:59.000000', NULL, 0),
