(4173955, 593790, 36065, '<td valign="top"><b>Hey there from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>First of all, congrats on a new personal, as well as a top 20 finish.<br/> <br/><b>Camera Work/Technical:</b> Terrific.  Your technical wok is one of the main strengths of the image.  Your focus is crisp, and your f/7 aperture kept the entire scene nicely focused.   <br/> <br/><b>Lighting:</b> I really like these types of shots, using flash to light your subject while relying on ambient light to light the scene.  I think that you had points deducted for the harsh shadows that were created on the right side of your group.  Adding a second flash would have remedied this easily.  I do like that the background is a bit less exposed than your subjects.<br/> <br/><b>Composition/Content:</b> Great content for the challenge, and you put together a nicely composed image.  Your placement of the group works nicely to draw the eye into the frame and right up the waterfall.<br/> <br/><b>My Opinion:</b> This image is appropriately scored.  While I like the lighting, I think that bringing up the exposure on the background would have worked to balance the image more, thus taking away the urge to think that this one was shot in studio, and may have even brought another tenth or two.  Nice work.<br/> <br/>Thank you for the opportunity to provide a critique on your entry,<br/><b>Eric</b> <br/></td>', 'Hey there from the Critique Club  First of all, congrats on a new personal, as well as a top 20 finish. Camera Work/Technical: Terrific.  Your technical wok is one of the main strengths of the image.  Your focus is crisp, and your f/7 aperture kept the entire scene nicely focused.    Lighting: I really like these types of shots, using flash to light your subject while relying on ambient light to light the scene.  I think that you had points deducted for the harsh shadows that were created on the right side of your group.  Adding a second flash would have remedied this easily.  I do like that the background is a bit less exposed than your subjects. Composition/Content: Great content for the challenge, and you put together a nicely composed image.  Your placement of the group works nicely to draw the eye into the frame and right up the waterfall. My Opinion: This image is appropriately scored.  While I like the lighting, I think that bringing up the exposure on the background would have worked to balance the image more, thus taking away the urge to think that this one was shot in studio, and may have even brought another tenth or two.  Nice work. Thank you for the opportunity to provide a critique on your entry,Eric ', '2007-10-17 04:19:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(4174271, 594202, 79720, '<td valign="top">I just came back to this shot to read some of the comments. I still think this was the most brilliant image of the challenge, one of the best I''ve seen in a while. The amount of work that went in to the setup alone is worth a ribbon.<br/> <br/>I''m quite certain the handful of low scores were people who felt this image to be "blasphemous", when in fact nothing could be further from the truth. Well done, and once again congratulations on a masterpiece.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-10-17 06:07:50.</i></td>', 'I just came back to this shot to read some of the comments. I still think this was the most brilliant image of the challenge, one of the best I''ve seen in a while. The amount of work that went in to the setup alone is worth a ribbon. I''m quite certain the handful of low scores were people who felt this image to be "blasphemous", when in fact nothing could be further from the truth. Well done, and once again congratulations on a masterpiece.', '2007-10-17 07:06:56.000000', '2007-10-17 07:07:50.000000', 0),
(4174288, 594413, 65713, '<td valign="top">Beautiful shot bringing several elements together well. Can understand peoples concerns during the challenge but it really is beautiful and think you can be proud of it regardless.</td>', 'Beautiful shot bringing several elements together well. Can understand peoples concerns during the challenge but it really is beautiful and think you can be proud of it regardless.', '2007-10-17 07:23:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(4175383, 593465, 32997, '<td valign="top">oh I am soooo glad you entered this...really it is horrible and wonderful, without this there is only a small box in which we can stick our shots...<br/></td>', 'oh I am soooo glad you entered this...really it is horrible and wonderful, without this there is only a small box in which we can stick our shots...', '2007-10-17 13:07:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(4175417, 594428, 40126, '<td valign="top">lovely faces. nice strong finish Sandy. (your comments are always encouraging).</td>', 'lovely faces. nice strong finish Sandy. (your comments are always encouraging).', '2007-10-17 13:19:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(4175440, 593790, 67585, '<td valign="top">Eric Thanks for the comment, really great of you to take the time.</td>', 'Eric Thanks for the comment, really great of you to take the time.', '2007-10-17 13:26:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(4176308, 594413, 49804, '<td valign="top">Wow, i absolutely love this shot, and love the take you had on the group portrait, sorry to see it score so low, i love it, it has amazing tones and killer composition, great job, added to faves</td>', 'Wow, i absolutely love this shot, and love the take you had on the group portrait, sorry to see it score so low, i love it, it has amazing tones and killer composition, great job, added to faves', '2007-10-17 18:33:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(4176775, 594428, 34659, '<td valign="top">Congrats on your top 10 finish with this terrific shot.  Great smiles and composition.  You''re right - you captured that friendship beautifully.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-10-17 21:05:05.</i></td>', 'Congrats on your top 10 finish with this terrific shot.  Great smiles and composition.  You''re right - you captured that friendship beautifully.', '2007-10-17 22:04:43.000000', '2007-10-17 22:05:05.000000', 0),
(4177601, 593815, 28742, '<td valign="top">You have a beautiful family, there Jennifer! Only overdone NI is on your youngest daughter. Still a great finish and a priceless keepsake.</td>', 'You have a beautiful family, there Jennifer! Only overdone NI is on your youngest daughter. Still a great finish and a priceless keepsake.', '2007-10-18 05:22:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(4185087, 592396, 61651, '<td valign="top">So, have you read up on that definition of "portrait" yet? ;)  Great take on the challenge, and I like the processing.</td>', 'So, have you read up on that definition of "portrait" yet? ;)  Great take on the challenge, and I like the processing.', '2007-10-21 14:55:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(4187742, 593016, 85550, '<td valign="top">CHEAP!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!</td>', 'CHEAP!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!', '2007-10-22 16:31:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(4188913, 594428, 48245, '<td valign="top">Very nice Sandy!</td>', 'Very nice Sandy!', '2007-10-23 01:23:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(4190285, 594741, 66384, '<td valign="top">I really like your b&amp;w conversion, and the use of b&amp;w for this subject seems very appropriate: a gray life of the graying women. What I love to see is that, except for the front woman, they all look so normal, bright eyed, and happy. I''m glad the voters appreciated it as it deserved.</td>', 'I really like your b&w conversion, and the use of b&w for this subject seems very appropriate: a gray life of the graying women. What I love to see is that, except for the front woman, they all look so normal, bright eyed, and happy. I''m glad the voters appreciated it as it deserved.', '2007-10-23 19:51:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(4190302, 594856, 66384, '<td valign="top">I was very interested by your comments about the pp trying to mimic the 3-D children''s books. I work on a laptop, and when I tilt the screen back (typically darkens the screen) the people and ball actually do seem to come right out of the picture. They brighten while the background darkens. <br/> <br/>I haven''t read the rest of the comments here, but I suspect your score was hurt by DNMC votes, since it is very atypical for a portrait. I think the image is very lively and a good shot.</td>', 'I was very interested by your comments about the pp trying to mimic the 3-D children''s books. I work on a laptop, and when I tilt the screen back (typically darkens the screen) the people and ball actually do seem to come right out of the picture. They brighten while the background darkens.  I haven''t read the rest of the comments here, but I suspect your score was hurt by DNMC votes, since it is very atypical for a portrait. I think the image is very lively and a good shot.', '2007-10-23 20:00:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(4193115, 594202, 84670, '<td valign="top">One of my favorite photos on this website.</td>', 'One of my favorite photos on this website.', '2007-10-24 16:41:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(4193876, 594202, 42567, '<td valign="top">...  I thought I was editing this post....guess not.  Look above this one :)<br/> <br/><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-10-24 21:33:47.</i></td>', '...  I thought I was editing this post....guess not.  Look above this one :) ', '2007-10-24 22:13:19.000000', '2007-10-24 22:33:47.000000', 0),
(4193899, 594202, 42567, '<td valign="top">I''ve seen and looked over this picture about 100 times.  I have only one problem with the picture.  I''ll get to that in a bit. <br/> <br/>I think the idea of Jesus hanging out with this group of people is great! Who is to say Leonardo Da Vinci painting is real or the truth.  Don''t be angre with me.  This is just my opinion!<br/> <br/>The problem I do have with this photo is the tattoos on Jesus.  I''m sorry but tattoos are a act of sin.  Jesus did not sin.  He was flawless unlike us.  I have three tattoos myself and I''m far from perfect! I have to say that I''m a huge Jesus freak!  I think mpeters said it best   "The followers of Christ were rough men, with a couple of exceptions. My reaction to your tatooed men is probably similar to the reaction of society to Jesus'' disciples.  <br/> <br/>But why Jesus tattooed?<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-10-24 21:38:59.</i></td>', 'I''ve seen and looked over this picture about 100 times.  I have only one problem with the picture.  I''ll get to that in a bit.  I think the idea of Jesus hanging out with this group of people is great! Who is to say Leonardo Da Vinci painting is real or the truth.  Don''t be angre with me.  This is just my opinion! The problem I do have with this photo is the tattoos on Jesus.  I''m sorry but tattoos are a act of sin.  Jesus did not sin.  He was flawless unlike us.  I have three tattoos myself and I''m far from perfect! I have to say that I''m a huge Jesus freak!  I think mpeters said it best   "The followers of Christ were rough men, with a couple of exceptions. My reaction to your tatooed men is probably similar to the reaction of society to Jesus'' disciples.   But why Jesus tattooed?', '2007-10-24 22:31:48.000000', '2007-10-24 22:38:59.000000', 0);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(4197132, 594902, 63398, '<td valign="top">Well, Jeffrey.....I have a problem with the portrait definition as it applies here. It''s a great different perspective shot, it''s decidedly an unusual angle.....I''m just glad to see by your own admission that it''s not a conventional portrait.</td>', 'Well, Jeffrey.....I have a problem with the portrait definition as it applies here. It''s a great different perspective shot, it''s decidedly an unusual angle.....I''m just glad to see by your own admission that it''s not a conventional portrait.', '2007-10-26 10:51:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(4197144, 594856, 63398, '<td valign="top">Well.....I should probably be fwapped! I gave this a three as I didn''t get the 3-D thing as it just seemed OOF and/or "funny" processing to me. It also IMO missed the mark for portrait. Please don''t hate me, I''m just trying to be honest with my obligatory comment.</td>', 'Well.....I should probably be fwapped! I gave this a three as I didn''t get the 3-D thing as it just seemed OOF and/or "funny" processing to me. It also IMO missed the mark for portrait. Please don''t hate me, I''m just trying to be honest with my obligatory comment.', '2007-10-26 10:55:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(4197163, 594803, 63398, '<td valign="top">I gave you a 4 just for sheer guts! No chance I would have DGed you for this! LOL!!!</td>', 'I gave you a 4 just for sheer guts! No chance I would have DGed you for this! LOL!!!', '2007-10-26 11:04:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(4197190, 594681, 63398, '<td valign="top">I gave this a 6 and was delighted to do so. They just look so HAPPY!!!! Great capture!</td>', 'I gave this a 6 and was delighted to do so. They just look so HAPPY!!!! Great capture!', '2007-10-26 11:17:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(4197208, 594543, 63398, '<td valign="top">Deb, I gave this a 6, cause, well, I saw what this was about and it seemed more of a tribute than a portrait, per se.....(Thereby negating my own weird DNMC policy). It''s a fine shot and I''m glad these guys were your port in the storm.</td>', 'Deb, I gave this a 6, cause, well, I saw what this was about and it seemed more of a tribute than a portrait, per se.....(Thereby negating my own weird DNMC policy). It''s a fine shot and I''m glad these guys were your port in the storm.', '2007-10-26 11:21:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(4197222, 592396, 63398, '<td valign="top">I *still* love this as a sterling example of the original group portrait. Kudos, Christian!</td>', 'I *still* love this as a sterling example of the original group portrait. Kudos, Christian!', '2007-10-26 11:24:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(4197291, 594803, 67697, '<td valign="top">What a scream... and to lose even because of U of M - ouchie!</td>', 'What a scream... and to lose even because of U of M - ouchie!', '2007-10-26 11:50:23.000000', NULL, 0),
